Prompt 3 - Apply the /code-review findings
------------------------------------------
Request:
  "once the code-review subagent is done, analyze the review and apply the
  suggestions to the code according to the review. summarize the changes
  and do not commit."
  (Prompt 2b, between these: "git checkout main && git merge
  post-hackathon-cleanup" - fast-forwarded main to the clean-up commit;
  not pushed.)

All 10 review findings were checked against the code and addressed:
  1. stage6_cluster_association.py: new SUMMARY_COLUMNS derived from
     ASSOCIATION_COLUMNS; the empty summary now has the same columns as a
     non-empty one (incl. p_value, permutations_used), so Stage 9 no longer
     fails when no SV-block pair is testable.
  2. cluster_inference.py: new VcfRecordError. Record-level parse errors fail
     immediately with "<chrom>:<pos>" instead of being mistaken for "index
     unavailable" and re-streaming the whole VCF. Real index failures on
     compressed input are logged at WARNING again (INFO for plain text).
  3. cluster_inference.py: streaming path skips any "#" line after #CHROM
     explicitly (defensive; such lines were already skipped by accident).
  4. cluster_inference.py: compression detected from gzip magic bytes
     (is_gzip_file/open_vcf_text) instead of the ".gz" suffix, so .vcf.bgz
     input works again.
  5. stage9_report.py: required-column checks now list every column
     build_facts uses (enrichment: haploblock_id, sv_type, p_value, flagged;
     PCA variance: component, explained_variance_ratio, n_variants).
  6. stage1_cluster_aware.py: check_metadata_matches_vcf() compares the VCF
     header samples (cluster_inference.read_vcf_samples) with the metadata
     before cluster inference starts, instead of after hours of inference.
     Metadata parsing factored into load_sample_metadata().
  7. stage_io.py: registered paths are resolved entry by entry; URLs inside
     per-chromosome maps are kept as-is; null/empty entries raise
     "paths.<name>.<chrom> is empty" instead of a TypeError traceback.
     read_tsv rejects a None path.
  8. stage6: log line now reports pairs actually tested vs. all pairs.
  9. stage_io.DEFAULT_BOUNDARY_DISTANCE_BP shared by Stage 1 (default) and
     Stage 2 (fallback) instead of two literal 5000s.
  10. stage7: config copy simplified to dict(config), comment added.

Tests: 6 new regression tests (Stage 1: metadata mismatch fails before
inference, .vcf.bgz + comment line, malformed record fails once with its
location; Stage 9: report with zero Stage 6 associations; new
test_stage_io.py: URL/relative path resolution, null path message).
Result: 40/40 pass, pyflakes clean, --test passes for Stages 1-9 with no
warnings. The malformed-record test was confirmed to fail when the fix is
reverted. Not committed.

